WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.360
Folks...

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.400
When you think of Japan, what’s the first
thing that comes to mind?

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:23.220
You may think of a modern and advanced country
with a rich culture...

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.380
Many will also think of manga, video games
or samurai...

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.500
Basically, you’ll likely have a very, very
positive image of the Land of the Rising Sun.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.250
However, as you know, all countries have positives
and negatives.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:42.060
Therefore, with this video, on VisualPolitik,
we’re going to talk about a subject that’s

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:50.670
hardly ever mentioned in the media: Japan’s
historical revisionism.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:57.310
But… what exactly does that mean?

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:02.239
See, we could say that revisionism is the
denial of historical events, usually negative,

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:11.250
of course, that happened in the past.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.850
Many countries that have had hard-to-digest
pasts strive to hide the truth, or try to

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.100
change the official version of the events.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.220
And Japan, is definitely one of them.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.250
Let's turn this around a bit…

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.180
When we think about Japan and its history,
what comes to mind?

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.780
Probably Samurai, geishas, perhaps the double
nuclear attack from the United States or,

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.630
the Pearl Harbor attack – at least because
of the movie.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:37.400
To us, knowing about these events is normal.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:43.440
But folks, do we really know how the Japanese
Empire was at the height of its power?

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.710
Do you know exactly what this means for the
Far East?

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:51.810
Why do you think that the countries that Japan
victimized, such as China or Korea, are still

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.820
very susceptible to this issue?

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.580
Listen up.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:07.610
(THE JAPANESE EMPIRE, THE EMPIRE OF TERROR)

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.479
You heard that right.

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:13.621
During the first half of the twentieth century
and, especially during the 30s and 40s, Japan

00:02:13.621 --> 00:02:17.830
was an imperialist power that dedicated itself
to invading neighboring countries as if there

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.830
were no tomorrow.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.360
And they did so without the slightest hint
of mercy.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.940
And when we say without mercy, we mean it,
it was truly inhumane.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:34.099
Throughout those years, Japanese troops committed
some of the most heinous abuses to human integrity,

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:36.850
life and the identity of people we could ever
imagine.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:42.750
Almost all of the worst things we could imagine
a country doing, Japan did to its colonies.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.690
We’re talking about terrible things, such
as enslaving people to work in Japan’s industries

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.720
and mining;
Enslaving women to work in brothels on the

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.970
war front,
not to mention the 731 squad experiments,

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.860
in which they used living people to conduct
chemical weapons experiments...

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.900
In the Chinese city of Nanjing alone, in barely
two months, the Japanese killed 300,000 people

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.510
and abused more than 80,000 women.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.709
It really gives you goosebumps.

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:14.050
Once it invaded a country, the Japanese empire
forcibly imposed its culture, its language

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.000
and Japan’s political and legal system.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.450
It even forced people to change their names.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:25.590
As you can see, we’re talking about a dark
era of uncontrolled and unlimited fear, atrocities

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.590
and violence.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.770
The soldiers and middle managers could do
as they wished.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:33.900
As a result of all this, at least twenty million
people in Asia lost their lives at the hands

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.630
of the Japanese Empire.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.990
Twenty million people!

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:47.281
In fact, the data on the Japanese army’s
lack of scruples during the war would give

00:03:47.281 --> 00:03:48.460
you goosebumps.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.640
Check this out, 40% of the American prisoners
of war who fell into the hands of the Japanese

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.379
didn’t survive.

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:55.379
40%!

00:03:55.379 --> 00:04:02.770
To give you an idea, in Europe that number
was less than 2%.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:05.330
And don’t think this was a coincidence,
not at all.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:10.569
The explanation lies in the ancient Japanese
culture known as bushido, a culture that despises

00:04:10.569 --> 00:04:12.110
soldiers who surrender in combat.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:16.590
This, folks, also explains why the Japanese
soldiers were so famous for fighting until

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.060
the very end.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:32.349
But... having said that, let’s close the
history book.

00:04:32.349 --> 00:04:36.779
Since Prime Minister Shinzo Abe’s rise to
power in 2012, Japan has surprised the world

00:04:36.779 --> 00:04:41.129
with a revision and denial policy of its history
that is very disturbing.

00:04:41.129 --> 00:04:42.129
But...

00:04:42.129 --> 00:04:43.129
What does it consist of?

00:04:43.129 --> 00:04:46.039
What is Shinzo Abe doing to change or sugar
coat the story?

00:04:46.039 --> 00:04:49.009
Are today's Japanese really aware of their
past?

00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:51.470
Listen up.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:05:00.490
(SHINZO ABE: REVISIONISM, IN THE INSTITUTIONS)

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:08.460
Shinzo Abe is already a well-known face.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:19.039
He’s been running Japan since 2012 and is
famous, particularly because of his economic

00:05:19.039 --> 00:05:27.000
policy program, better known as Abenomics.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:42.719
Now, there’s a much more controversial aspect
to Shinzo Abe that isn’t mentioned much

00:05:42.719 --> 00:05:45.999
in the West: Abe is an openly convinced revisionist.

00:05:45.999 --> 00:05:55.089
And the truth is that he’s always been one.

00:05:55.089 --> 00:05:59.740
Since he first entered the Diet, Japan’s
parliament, in 1993, Abe has promoted laws

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:04.610
and reforms that seek to sugar coat how the
history of the Japanese Empire is shown to

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:05.610
society.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:10.699
For example, in his first and brief term as
Prime Minister, between September 2006 and

00:06:10.699 --> 00:06:14.929
September 2007, Abe approved a Fundamental
Law of Education reform to establish a more

00:06:14.929 --> 00:06:20.229
patriotic vision with more traditionalist
moral values in the Japanese education system.

00:06:20.229 --> 00:06:24.069
That is, Pure Nationalism in Education System.

00:06:24.069 --> 00:06:26.349
And not just that.

00:06:26.349 --> 00:06:30.929
Shinzo Abe himself is a member of Nippon Kaigi,
a Japanese ultra-nationalist group founded

00:06:30.929 --> 00:06:36.869
in 1997 that openly defends historical revisionism
to exculpate the Japanese Empire from its

00:06:36.869 --> 00:06:37.869
crimes.

00:06:37.869 --> 00:06:42.539
Basically, it’s as if Angela Merkel belonged
to an ultra-radical far-right group in Germany.

00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:45.779
But, do you think Abe hides his involvement?

00:06:45.779 --> 00:06:47.300
Not at all.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:51.179
(U.S. Textbook Skews History, Prime Minister
of Japan Says.

00:06:51.179 --> 00:06:54.210
The New York Times)

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:58.770
In fact, folks, Prime Minister Abe not only
modified the Japanese Education Law to change

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:04.020
educational content, but also openly criticizes
how Japan's history is addressed in other

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.020
countries.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.710
Basically, makes no effort to conceal his
bias.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:11.070
(Abe's revisionism nets own goals at home
and away.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.379
The Japan Times)

00:07:12.379 --> 00:07:16.990
The Japanese Prime Minister even attacked
the McGraw-Hill publishing house for the description

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:20.720
they made of how Japan forced women to prostitute
themselves on the war front.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.610
Women who, for him and the revisionists, were
nothing more than volunteers who earned a

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:28.939
lot of money, although all the historical
evidence claims they were slaves.

00:07:28.939 --> 00:07:33.939
("I just looked at a document, McGraw-Hill's
textbook, and I was shocked.

00:07:33.939 --> 00:07:38.659
This kind of textbook is being used in the
United States, as we did not protest the things

00:07:38.659 --> 00:07:42.599
we should have, or we failed to correct the
things we should have."

00:07:42.599 --> 00:07:45.249
Shinzo Abe, Japan's Prime Minister)

00:07:45.249 --> 00:07:47.369
And this wasn’t an isolated case...

00:07:47.369 --> 00:07:52.469
Abe's Japan began when he started implanting
the most extreme revisionism in the institutions,

00:07:52.469 --> 00:08:00.620
driven by the ultra-nationalist group Nippon
Kaigi.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.300
In his speech during the 70th anniversary
of Japan's surrender, Abe, citing the 3 million

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:10.199
who died in the Japanese Empire, extolled
their sacrifices and called them valuable.

00:08:10.199 --> 00:08:14.479
At the very same event, by the way, the then
Emperor Akihito also spoke.He, of course,

00:08:14.479 --> 00:08:18.779
is Hirohito’ son, the Emperor who attacked
Pearl Harbor and unleashed so many wars across

00:08:18.779 --> 00:08:19.779
Asia.

00:08:19.779 --> 00:08:24.250
Well, in contrast to Shinzo Abe, Akihito was
somewhat more embarrassed by his country’s

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:25.250
revisionist inclination.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:31.219
(“Our country today enjoys peace and prosperity,
thanks to the ceaseless efforts made by the

00:08:31.219 --> 00:08:36.600
people of Japan toward recovery from the devastation
of the war and toward development, always

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:40.760
backed by their earnest desire for the continuation
of peace.”

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.509
Emperor Akihito)

00:08:43.509 --> 00:08:50.160
It’s curious that the Emperor himself had
a much more conciliatory speech than the prime

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:57.120
minister regarding the empire's past... don't
you think?

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.410
Well, there’s more.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:06.110
Both Shinzo Abe and many of his party’s
ministers, deputies and senators regularly

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:10.060
visit or send offerings to the Yasukuni Shrine.

00:09:10.060 --> 00:09:17.140
Yasukuni, folks, is a Shinto shrine where
14 class A war criminals from the Japanese

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.779
Empire, among others, are honored.

00:09:18.779 --> 00:09:22.650
War criminals that were declared as such in
the Tokyo Trials, the Japanese equivalent

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:24.630
to the Nuremberg Trials for the Nazis.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:29.930
But, folks, if you think this is all a matter
or speeches, words and visits to controversial

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:33.430
places, you’re very, very mistaken.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:37.560
Listen up.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:43.649
(THE DREAM OF CONTROLLING EDUCATION)

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:45.160
That's right folks, it's no secret.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:49.990
Every ruler who aspires to change history,
for better or for worse, needs to influence

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:53.220
education.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:57.370
We already mentioned that Abe modified the
educational law for this purpose, but he didn’t

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.370
stop there.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:02.700
One of his government’s biggest scandals
was that of the Osaka Moritomo Gakuen's nursery

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.700
school.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.709
See, this private kindergarten school, which
has an ultra-nationalist ideology, - yes,

00:10:07.709 --> 00:10:14.139
a nursery school - indoctrinated children
in the purest Japanese Empire style.

00:10:14.139 --> 00:10:19.690
They even made them memorize the so-called
Imperial Rescript on Education of 1890 every

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.970
day, a kind of manifesto with the Empire’s
principles.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.300
For five and six year-olds!

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:31.600
But, just a second, what does Shinzo Abe have
to do with all this?

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.389
Well, in addition to publicly stating that
he shared the vision of the director, Yasunori

00:10:35.389 --> 00:10:39.319
Kagoike, Abe and his wife, who by the way
was named honorary director of the nursery,

00:10:39.319 --> 00:10:44.040
were immersed in a donations and favoritism
scandal where public land was sold to benefit

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.040
the nursery.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.220
The corruption scandal almost brought down
Abe's government, although he managed to remain

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:51.300
standing in the end.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:57.379
But, folks, besides the imperialist nursery
scandal, there’s a kind of historical whitewash

00:10:57.379 --> 00:11:00.430
throughout Japan’s entire educational system.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:05.540
History teacher Tamaki Matsuoka, famous for
having got 250 former soldiers from the time

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:10.189
of the Japanese Empire to admit to multiple
war crimes, is an expert in analyzing how

00:11:10.189 --> 00:11:12.000
Japan's past is tackled in modern schools.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.000
And folks, his conclusions are very discouraging.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:16.950
Matsuoka accuses the government of deliberately
silencing the most negative historical events

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:20.320
of the Japanese Empire.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:24.779
For example, in the textbooks that students
use in schools, only one footnote is dedicated

00:11:24.779 --> 00:11:28.230
to the Nanking massacre, which we talked about
at the beginning of this video.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:35.389
What can I say, 300,000 victims seems enough
to become a relevant fact in history books,

00:11:35.389 --> 00:11:36.389
don't you think?

00:11:36.389 --> 00:11:39.970
But, the fact that this is happening raises
an essential question;, what effects could

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.920
this historical silencing have?

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:50.220
Folks, even though here on VISUALPOLITIK we
don’t really like looking too far back,

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:55.500
ignoring such an important part of history
can be dangerous when making political decisions.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.790
Especially in a region of the world that has
so many national feelings.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:03.300
To make matters worse, movies, books and series
that the Japanese government itself promotes,

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:07.339
feed this idea of ​​changing people’s
vision of the past.

00:12:07.339 --> 00:12:12.199
I’m referring to works such as The Eternal
Zero, a film that highlights the importance

00:12:12.199 --> 00:12:13.199
of the Kamikaze pilots,

00:12:13.199 --> 00:12:17.580
The case is that this growing nationalism,
along with the political and commercial confrontations

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.980
that have been registered in this area of
​​the world, help explain the growing

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:25.009
suspicion with which young Japanese people
have begun looking at their neighbors.

00:12:25.009 --> 00:12:29.579
Sociological studies state that today 80%
of Japanese people have a bad image of China,

00:12:29.579 --> 00:12:31.100
and 60% of South Korea.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.220
And that’s obviously not a good thing.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:38.069
Folks, after knowing all this, what do you
think about the way in which Japan is dealing

00:12:38.069 --> 00:12:39.069
with its past?

00:12:39.069 --> 00:12:40.670
Do you think this could have consequences?

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:44.149
Maybe Japan should learn from Germany about
facing up to its history?

